From: Max Bretschneider <max.bretschneider@leica-geosystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov08d10: avoid reading the unset mode in probe debug

The hardware-configuration check runs before probe assigns cur_mode. Use the
validated endpoint lane count in the debug message. With dynamic debugging
enabled the old argument dereferences NULL.

Adapted to the retained Linux 7.3.1 source from the author's v2 patch 1/4:
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/20261024-ov08d10-get-selection-v2-1-f8c49972ca18@leica-geosystems.com/
The original GPL-2.0 and Intel attribution are retained. No sensor register,
power sequence, board address or mode table is changed.

Signed-off-by: Max Bretschneider <max.bretschneider@leica-geosystems.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c
@@ -1431,7 +1431,8 @@ static int ov08d10_get_hwcfg(struct ov08d10 *ov08d10)
 		goto check_hwcfg_error;
 	}
 
-	dev_dbg(dev, "Using %u data lanes\n", ov08d10->cur_mode->data_lanes);
+	dev_dbg(dev, "Using %u data lanes\n",
+		bus_cfg.bus.mipi_csi2.num_data_lanes);
 
 	ov08d10->priv_lane = &lane_cfg_2;
 	ov08d10->modes_size = ov08d10_modes_num(ov08d10);
